   "source": [
    "# Overview: Aging mouse brain SpiderNet workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook presents an end-to-end workflow for applying **SpiderNet** to the aging mouse brain dataset, starting from the processed bundle generated by **`spidernet_dataloading_MIdimselection_AgingBrain`**, through model training, result export, biological interpretation, and age-related downstream analyses. The goal is to identify spatial meta-interactions (MIs) from the tissue, characterize the sender--receiver communication programs captured by these MIs, and evaluate how selected interaction patterns relate to local aging signals and predicted age-associated tissue states.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What this notebook does\n",
    "1. Define dataset-specific paths, metadata, and preprocessing/training settings\n",
    "2. Reuse the preprocessed AgingBrain SpiderNet bundle generated by `spidernet_dataloading_MIdimselection_AgingBrain`\n",
    "3. Build and train the SpiderNet model\n",
    "4. Export inferred cell--cell meta-interactions and associated loading matrices\n",
    "5. Interpret the learned MIs by examining MI-associated ligand--receptor pairs, sender/receiver gene programs, and sender--receiver cell-type enrichment patterns\n",
    "6. Perform age-related downstream analyses, including:\n",
    "   - cell-level age prediction based on inferred interaction features,\n",
    "   - visualization of spatial activity patterns for selected MIs,\n",
    "   - evaluation of age-associated signaling across cell types and tissue context,\n",
    "   - in silico perturbation analyses to assess the predicted local impact of selected cell populations or interaction programs\n",
    "   - GO enrichment analysis of MI-associated sender/receiver gene programs\n"
   ]
  },
